            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 75-year-old man came to the clinic because of pain and weakness in his legs. He had fallen a year earlier. The pain and weakness were caused by a bilateral rupture of the tendon of the M. rectus femoris.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
